      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHITE KEYS (2) has a strong record this track and trip with two wins and two placings from five starts. Was out of the placings last time (29.85) at this track in a Grade 4/5, finishing fourth and beaten 4.5 lengths. With a clean break looks hard to beat. NASH MASH (7) stalked the lead from a middle draw and boxed on well to finish 2.5 lengths back in second (29.86) at this track in a Grade 5/6 over 509m. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card last start despite being beaten. Expected to be in the finish again. SUNSET PARIS (1) copped a check in the run last time and never threatened when fifth (30.32) in a Grade 4/5 at this track. Better than last start and can bounce back. TRANSCRIPT (8) generally performs well from this box.",
